---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_116",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 116,
  "text": "[[386.1]] <b>96.  De methodo synthetica aut anagogica applicanda in algebra [Frühjahr 1680 (?)]</b>\n [[386.3]] <tab/>[Frühjahr 1680 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[386.10]] Methodus synthetica est, cum problema difficile soluturi incipimus a facilioribus. In\n[[386.11]] synthesi per se facili observandum, ut tentemus obtinere elegantes progressiones, quibus\n[[386.12]] Tabularum calculandarum compendia contineantur. Algebra, qua scilicet incognitum pro\n[[386.13]] cognito sumimus, est synthesis quaedam peculiaris problematis propositi, fictitia. Synthesis\n[[386.14]] fictitia generalis, cum generalis expressio habetur rei quae quaeritur, ut in curvis\n[[386.15]] communibus. </p>\n<p> [[386.16]] Analysis pura quae nihil syntheseos habet, est Anagogica, in qua semper procedimus\n[[386.17]] per incognita retro, nempe reducendo problema propositum ad aliud facilius, et hoc\n[[386.18]] iterum ad aliud. Talis est Methodus mea qua utor cum alias aequationes reduco ad\n[[386.19]] aequicompositas, item cum formulas in quibus potentiae, reduco ad illas in quibus sola\n[[386.20]] rectangula. Item cum curvarum ordinatas resolvo in partes seu in duas pluresve ordinatas\n[[386.21]] aliarum curvarum simpliciorum; vel terminos seriei, in plurium serierum terminos, quo\n[[386.22]] facto summam vel dimensionem illarum reduco ad has simpliciores. Eademque methodo\n[[386.23]] pervenio ad seriem summatricem quando aliqua per formulam communem exprimibilis\n[[386.24]] datur, quando scilicet formula resolvitur in differentiam duorum terminorum vicinorum\n[[386.25]] ejusdem seriei. </p>\n<p> [[386.26]] Methodus procedendi per meras cognitas est pure synthetica. Mixtas mixta. <i>Zetetica</i>\n[[386.27]] Vietae pertinent ad Synthesin, est enim percurrere pulchriora problemata. Huc pertinent\n[[387.1]] et factiones Canonicae, seu constructiones quaedam crebro utiles, nam quando forte\n[[387.2]] incidimus in elegantem constructionem, hanc notamus, ut postea jam ad alia applicemus.\n[[387.3]] Est tamen his mixta quaedam Anagogica, dum alia problemata ad ista solennia reducuntur. </p>\n<p> [[387.5]] Data veterum pertinent ad Anagogicam, ut appareat ex problematis recessibus, ex\n[[387.6]] datis quaenam sequantur; et ita problema reducemus ad aliud. Exemplum elegans praebet\n[[387.7]] solutio problematum quorundam quae Batavus proposuit, Monfortius Neapolitanus solvit\n[[387.8]] numerice, ego reduxi ad problemata alia jam constructa. Eadem Methodo tractabitur\n[[387.9]] utiliter problema quod mihi proposuit Fergusonius. Ex duobus punctis <i>A, B</i> datis duas\n[[387.10]] [rectas] ad idem punctum circuli <i>C</i> ita\n[[387.11]] ducere ut comprehensae intra circulum\n[[387.12]] sint aequales. Nam si <i>CD</i>, et <i>CE</i> aequales\n[[387.13]] erit triangulum <i>CDE</i> isosceles. Per\n[[387.14]] punctum <i>C</i> ducatur parallela ipsi <i>DE</i>,\n[[387.15]] nempe <i>FCG</i>, ea circulum tanget, ergo\n[[387.16]] problema habemus simplicius, nam\n[[387.17]] omissa ipsarum <i>CD, CE</i> mentione, tantum\n[[387.18]] quaeritur punctum circuli <i>C</i> tale, ut\n[[387.19]] ex datis punctis <i>A, B</i> ad ipsum ductae\n[[387.20]] rectae faciant angulos ad tangentem aequales, nam ut angulus <i>D</i> aequ. angulo <i>E</i>, ita et\n[[387.21]] angulus <i>ACF</i> aequ. angulo <i>BCG</i>. Itaque res reducta ad hoc problema Catoptricum jam ab\n[[387.22]] aliis solutum. Invenire punctum circuli <i>C</i> quod radium a dato puncto <i>C</i> venientem, ad\n[[387.23]] aliud datum <i>B</i> reflectat. Vel quod eodem redit datis duobus focis <i>A, B</i> describere Ellipsin\n[[387.24]] quae datum circulum <i>CDE</i> tangat et invenire punctum contactus. </p>\n<p> [[387.25]] Notandum quod problemata ideo fiunt difficilia, quod non satis determinata, haec\n[[387.26]] etiam causa irrationalitatis, nam semper in irrationali plures radices. </p>\n",
  "number": "96.",
  "title": "De methodo synthetica aut anagogica applicanda in algebra",
  "date": "[Frühjahr 1680 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:96. De methodo synthetica aut anagogica applicanda in algebra [Frühjahr 1680 (?)] [Frühjahr 1680 (?)] Methodus synthetica est, cum problema difficile soluturi incipimus a facilioribus. In synthesi per se facili observandum, ut tentemus obtinere elegantes progressiones, quibus Tabularum calculandarum...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>